Negative control for the scene rail's own row (`R7-8`).

Puts the rail back inside the controls row, beside the transport, and takes the
full-width row away with it — the same rail, the same stops, the same seek — so
the only claim that can go red is the ruled one: the rail is a SIBLING of the
bar, not another instrument crammed into it. Inline it shares the row with the
menu, the transport and the sheet toggle, which is what squashed five Gherkin
sentences into truncated fragments in the operator's screenshot; and the armed
track loses the one place wide enough to write its whole name.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the scene-rail placement case — the rail is a child of the bar's root and
NOT of its controls row, it takes the page's own width, and the armed track is
named at its head.

